                        <field name="dc_description">Printed for the author, by John Jones, 40, South Great George's St., and published at the office, no. 10, Eden-Quay, ten doors below Carlile Bridge. -- At foot of title: "also, remarks on the inevitable consequences of granting political power to the Roman Catholics. - The similarity of the present politics to those which preceded former rebellions and massaces, proved from history. - The modern demagogues unmasked. Mr. Plunkett's official career review : his late insult to our city grand jury particularly considerer  the bottle and rattle-farce placed in a proper light : a similiar proceeding of an Attorney-General in 1713, condemned by the Parliament. - Ribbonism first discovered by the Rev. Mr. Hamilton, of Roscrea, in 1814, &c. &c.". -- Price: one shilling and three-pence. -- Includes advertisement addressed to "the loyal supporters of the constitution". -- Dedicated "to the loyal Protestants of Ireland. -- Includes errata. </field>
